Note that $\frac{F_{n+1}}{F_n F_{n+2}} = \frac{F_{n+1}}{F_n F_{n+1}+F_n^2} = \frac{1}{F_n+F_{n+1}}.$
We will now manipulate this expression to recognize a telescoping series. We can rewrite this as $\frac{1}{F_n + F_{n+1}} = \frac{F_{n+2}-F_n}{F_n(F_{n+2} - F_n)} = \frac{F_{n+2}-F_n}{F_{n+2}F_n} = \frac{1}{F_n}-\frac{1}{F_{n+2}}.$
It follows that \begin{align*}
\sum_{n=1}^\infty \frac{F_{n+1}}{F_n F_{n+2}} &= \sum_{n=1}^\infty \frac{1}{F_n}-\frac{1}{F_{n+2}} = \left(\frac{1}{F_1}-\frac{1}{F_2}\right)+\left(\frac{1}{F_2}-\frac{1}{F_3}\right) + \ldots\\
&= \frac{1}{F_1}-\frac{1}{F_{\infty}} = \boxed{\frac{1}{1}-\frac{1}{F_{\infty}} = 1 - \frac{1}{F_{\infty}}.}
\end{align*}
However, it can be shown that $\displaystyle \lim_{n\to\infty} \frac{F_{n+1}}{F_n} = \varphi$ (where $\varphi = \frac{1 + \sqrt{5}}{2}$), so that $\displaystyle \lim_{n\to\infty} F_{n+1} = \lim_{n\to\infty} \varphi F_n.$ It follows that $\displaystyle \lim_{n\to\infty} F_{n+2} = \lim_{n\to\infty} \varphi F_{n+1} = \varphi^2 F_n,$ so $\displaystyle \lim_{n\to\infty} \frac{F_{n+2}}{F_n} = \varphi^2,$ so $\displaystyle \lim_{n\to\infty} \frac{1}{F_{n+2}} = \frac{1}{\varphi^2 F_n} = \frac{\varphi^2}{\varphi^4} \frac{1}{F_n} = \frac{1}{\varphi F_n},$ and so \begin{align*}
1 - \frac{1}{F_{\infty}} &= 1 - \lim_{n\to\infty} \frac{1}{F_n} = 1 - \frac{1}{\varphi}.
\end{align*}
